<<~ ahu slot=`#/contract`>>

! LarDiskProjector ~ the node hand on the projection law

''The law lives at'' `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection` — two surfaces, bag roles,
carrier-whole granularity, routing, the write ward. This carrier names what the enacting file owns on
top of that law, and nothing the law already states.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/law`>>

!! What the projector itself binds

# ''One render shore.'' `carrierFileFn` — the VM's `exportCarrierFile` — returns the carrier's own
filetype as bytes plus extension, and the projector only sites the result at `<uri-path><ext>` (plus
a `.meta` sidecar where the type calls for one). A null answer skips the write. The VM registry
decides type and bytes; the projector decides nothing about either.
# ''The reads compare, never source.'' The projector opens files to answer two questions: //do these
bytes already match//, and //may this file leave//. No byte it reads reaches a record. A file that
fails to read never reads as equal: the byte skip falls through to the gate, which decides, and at an
unlink the file stays.
# ''An unlink needs a holding answer and a reading.'' A cross-mirror unlink weighs a file only where
`bagsHolding` reports the carrier gone from that bag — a true MOVE or promotion. A carrier still held
there, a working edit SHADOWING its canon copy, keeps its file. Without that callback every other
mirror's files get weighed by path, so its absence widens the sweep. Every file weighed, at every
unlink, then meets one judge (`judgeHome`, under `settleHomes`): it leaves only where its bytes stand
agreed, and a file that holds a hand's words stays while the carrier stands off (the law:
`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection#/projection-law`, an unlink reads the file first).
# ''A base names a home only where its mirror may write.'' The base's `path` remembers an earlier
home across a restart, and the ingest gesture pins a base at whatever source it read, in a row of its own beside the mirror's. `basedHomes`
passes each such path through the mirror's own ward (`confineMirrorWrite`: the mirror's root, or a file
directly in the bags root under `allowBagsRootFiles`): a path the ward would refuse names no home, so a source kept
in a holding directory beside the mirror never meets the judge and never leaves.
# ''A stem match binds the WHOLE stem.'' `carrierDiskFiles` resolves a carrier's actual files by the
full extension-less stem plus one extension segment, so a sibling carrier sharing only a prefix never
gets swept. A missing directory reads as no files.
# ''The in-flight set carries no correctness.'' The content-hash gates hold the echo law — ingest
drops a disk-hash matching its synced-hash, projection skips a byte-identical write. The `writing`
set survives beneath them as latency optimization alone: it spares a stat on our own in-flight write,
and every guarantee stands without it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-servo`>>

!! The level-triggered reconcile gate

This section, anchored `#/the-servo`, holds the disk shore's level-triggered reconcile gate, its teardown and its measure; no servo and no timer stand in it.

`LarDiskProjector.start` keys the timer-free `KeyedReconcileGate` by carrier root; a child change climbs `$fragment-parent` to that root. A clean mark queues one reconcile, a queued mark changes nothing, and a mark during a running reconcile makes the key run once more on completion. M marks to one key cost at most M + 1 reconciles, and no mark storm starves a key. One drain owns the queue until it empties, reconciling keys one at a time in first-marked order and yielding to the host between reconciles. The mount scan marks mirror-backed roots in the same synchronous turn as change-bus subscription; the first reconcile starts in a microtask. Each reconcile reads settled wiki state. The unsubscribe removes the listener and awaits `stop()`, which stops admission, drops waiting work, and waits for a running reconcile. The Synced tree holds nothing to flush: each observation rests as it gets recorded. The measure fields count change events, elapsed time from the last change event to the first file write, `bagsHolding` calls in that window, and file writes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/edges`>>

